q(7,[c('a · Beetle–disk system angular momentum magnitude','Unchanged.',['Increases.','Decreases.'],'There is no external axial torque; the beetle and disk exchange angular momentum internally.'),c('b · Beetle angular momentum and angular speed magnitudes','Both increase.',['Both decrease.','Angular momentum increases while angular speed decreases.'],'At fixed radius the beetle has constantI, and walking with the rotation transfers angular momentum to it.'),c('c · Disk angular momentum and angular speed magnitudes','Both decrease.',['Both increase.','Both remain unchanged.'],'The disk gives the beetle angular momentum, with constantdisk inertia.'),c('d · Walking against rotation','System unchanged; disk speeds up; beetle magnitudes decrease until zero, then increase if it reverses.',['System angular momentum decreases; disk slows down.','System unchanged; both beetle and disk must speed up in the same direction.'],'Signed beetle angular momentum decreases and disk angular momentum increases. A magnitude decreases only until the beetle reaches zero angular velocity; the source does not bound its walking speed.')],'Take the initial disk direction aspositive. Conservation gives ΔL_disk=−ΔL_beetle. For the usual case where the beetle still moves counterclockwise in the lab, part(d) means beetle decreases and disk increases; the option states the full reversal caveat.',[25,26])
